<!--
The entry the wasm binary runs: a headless behavior tree that logs a greeting
and exits. It uses only `web`-feature types (`Sequence`/`Log`/`CallOnReady`), so it
runs in a `--features web` wasm build with no extra registration.

The page names it as its launch, `<Wasm repo="/examples/wasm" main="hello.bsx"/>`:
the browser process reads `hello.bsx` out of the served repo and boots it exactly
as the native binary boots its `--main`. Any `.bsx` whose tags are compiled into
the wasm binary runs the same way; build the wasm with more features to run richer
examples.

    beet --main=examples/wasm/hello.bsx   # the same entry, natively
-->
<Sequence {CallOnReady}>
	<Log message="Hello from beet, running headless in your browser."/>
	<Log message="This entry was compiled to wasm and read from the served repo store."/>
	<Log message="Edit examples/wasm/hello.bsx and the page live-reloads."/>
</Sequence>
